 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Неуклюжий бармен  (The Clumsy Bartender)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "kostya": "Костя"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Kostya walks up to Barinov's table at the restaurant with a plan: swap the wrong bottle for a safe one without explaining why. Barinov has no patience for it. Listen for how fast the chef runs out of it.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Мне нужна эта бутылка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "О чём ты говоришь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я возьму эту бутылку.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "А вам поставлю другую.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечего делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Нет, я просто хочу дать другую.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не трогай ничего, иди отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Но я должен её забрать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я сказал, иди отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, извините, я пойду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the bottle swap, up close.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Excuse me, have a pleasant evening.' A wish hides an unspoken 'I wish you', so the evening takes the 'of' endings: \"priyatnogo vechera\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do you want from me?' \"Chto tebe nuzhno?\", 'what to you is needed?'. \"Ot menya\", from me.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Мне нужна эта бутылка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I need this bottle.' \"Nuzhna\" matches the bottle, which is feminine; for a knife it would be \"nuzhen\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "О чём ты говоришь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What are you on about?' To the bartender the chef says \"ty govorish\"; to the new boss it was \"vy govorite\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я возьму эту бутылку.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'll take this bottle.' \"Vozmu\", I'll take, belongs to \"vzyat\", even though the two look quite different.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "А вам поставлю другую.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And I'll put another one out for you.' \"Postavlyu\" is literally 'I'll stand': bottles are stood, not laid. \"Vam\", for you, is polite.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечего делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Have you got nothing better to do?' \"Nechego delat\", nothing to do: \"ne\" and \"chego\" fused into one word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Нет, я просто хочу дать другую.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I just want to give you another one.' \"Prosto\", just, simply. \"Dat\", to give.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не трогай ничего, иди отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't touch anything, get out of here!' Russian stacks the 'not': \"ne trogay nichego\", 'don't touch nothing'. \"Otsyuda\", from here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Но я должен её забрать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But I have to take it.' \"Eyo\", her: the bottle is a she in Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я сказал, иди отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I said, get out!' \"Idi\", go!, is the friendly-form command from \"idti\", to go on foot. Said twice, it's an order.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, извините, я пойду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, sorry, I'll go.' \"Izvinite\" is the polite sorry; to a friend it would be \"izvini\". Now hear him get sent packing, start to end.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
   "gap": 0.5
